## Spring Data JPA Implementation (Default)

```java
package org.springframework.samples.petclinic.repository.springdatajpa;

import org.springframework.context.annotation.Profile;
import org.springframework.data.jpa.repository.Query;
import org.springframework.data.repository.Repository;
import org.springframework.data.repository.query.Param;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.model.Entity;
import org.springframework.samples.petclinic.repository.EntityRepository;

import java.util.Collection;

@Profile("spring-data-jpa")  // REQUIRED - activates only with this profile
public interface SpringDataEntityRepository extends EntityRepository, Repository<Entity, Integer> {

    @Override
    @Query("SELECT DISTINCT e FROM Entity e LEFT JOIN FETCH e.children WHERE e.id = :id")
    Entity findById(@Param("id") int id);

    @Override
    @Query("SELECT e FROM Entity e WHERE e.fieldName LIKE :value%")
    Collection<Entity> findByFieldName(@Param("value") String value);
    
    // findAll(), save(), delete() are auto-implemented by Spring Data
}
```

---

## CRITICAL RULES

### Rule 1: Always Use @Profile Annotation
```java
@Profile("spring-data-jpa")  // Required for Spring Data implementations
public interface SpringDataEntityRepository extends EntityRepository, Repository<Entity, Integer> {
```

### Rule 2: Use LEFT JOIN FETCH for Relationships
Avoid N+1 query problems:
```java
// ❌ Bad - causes N+1 queries
@Query("SELECT o FROM Owner o WHERE o.id = :id")
Owner findById(@Param("id") int id);

// ✅ Good - eager fetches in one query
@Query("SELECT o FROM Owner o LEFT JOIN FETCH o.pets WHERE o.id = :id")
Owner findById(@Param("id") int id);
```

### Rule 3: Use Named Parameters
```java
// ❌ Bad - positional parameters
@Query("SELECT o FROM Owner o WHERE o.lastName LIKE ?1%")
Collection<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName);

// ✅ Good - named parameters with @Param
@Query("SELECT o FROM Owner o WHERE o.lastName LIKE :lastName%")
Collection<Owner> findByLastName(@Param("lastName") String lastName);
```

### Rule 4: Return Collection<> Not List<>
```java
// ✅ Flexible return type
Collection<Owner> findAll() throws DataAccessException;
Collection<Owner> findByLastName(String lastName) throws DataAccessException;
```

### Rule 5: Throw DataAccessException
```java
Entity findById(int id) throws DataAccessException;
void save(Entity entity) throws DataAccessException;
```

